{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/bitnami/git","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:07:31.445Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/bitnami/git/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/bitnami/git"},"readme":"# Bitnami Secure Image for Git\n\n> Git is an open source distributed version control system that can handle both small and large projects with speed and efficiency.\n\n[Overview of Git](https://git-scm.com/)\nTrademarks: This software listing is packaged by Bitnami. The respective trademarks mentioned in the offering are owned by the respective companies, and use of them does not imply any affiliation or endorsement.\n\n## <a id=\"tl-dr\"></a> TL;DR\n\n```console\ndocker run --name git REGISTRY_NAME/bitnami/git:latest\n```\n\n> Note: You need to substitute the `REGISTRY_NAME` placeholder with a reference to your container registry.\n\n## <a id=\"supported-tags-and-respective-dockerfile\"></a> Supported tags and respective `Dockerfile` links\n\nLearn more about the Bitnami tagging policy and the difference between rolling tags and immutable tags [in our documentation page](https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-tanzu/application-catalog/tanzu-application-catalog/services/tac-doc/apps-tutorials-understand-rolling-tags-containers-index.html).\n\n## <a id=\"get-this-image\"></a> Get this image\n\nThe Bitnami Git Docker image is only available to [Bitnami Secure Images](https://bitnami.com) customers.\n\n## <a id=\"configuration\"></a> Configuration\n\nThe following section describes how to run commands\n\n### <a id=\"running-commands\"></a> Running commands\n\nTo run commands inside this container you can use `docker run`, for example to execute `git version` you can follow below example\n\n```console\ndocker run --name git REGISTRY_NAME/bitnami/git:latest git --version\n```\n\n### <a id=\"fips-configuration-in-bitnami-secure\"></a> FIPS configuration in Bitnami Secure Images\n\nThe Bitnami Git Docker image from the [Bitnami Secure Images](https://go-vmware.broadcom.com/contact-us) catalog includes extra features and settings to configure the container with FIPS capabilities. You can configure the next environment variables:\n\n- `OPENSSL_FIPS`: whether OpenSSL runs in FIPS mode or not. `yes` (default), `no`.\n\n## <a id=\"notable-changes\"></a> Notable Changes\n\n### <a id=\"starting-january-16-2024\"></a> Starting January 16, 2024\n\n- The `docker-compose.yaml` file has been removed, as it was solely intended for internal testing purposes.\n\n### <a id=\"2-31-0-debian-10\"></a> 2.31.0-debian-10-r2\n\n- The `ENTRYPOINT` of the container has been modified to load a proper NSS environment that enables git ssh connections when running the container as non-root.\n- The `CMD` is also changed to enter the Bash shell.\n\nIf you were using the container without replacing the entrypoint, make sure you specify the `git` command now:\n\n```diff\n-docker run REGISTRY_NAME/bitnami/git:latest --version\n+docker run REGISTRY_NAME/bitnami/git:latest git --version\n```\n\n## <a id=\"license\"></a> License\n\nCopyright &copy; 2026 Broadcom. The term \"Broadcom\" refers to Broadcom Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.\n\nLicensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");\nyou may not use this file except in compliance with the License.\nYou may obtain a copy of the License at\n\n<http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0>\n\nUnless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\ndistributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\nWITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\nSee the License for the specific language governing permissions and\nlimitations under the License.","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"bitnami","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/bitnami","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2018-10-25T14:54:22.805516Z","updated":"2026-09-25T07:55:12.957251Z","categories":["Developer tools"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":46432688,"stars":54},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","application/vnd.oci.image.config.v1+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","application/vnd.vmware.tac.metadata.config.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image","unrecognized"],"storage":499155305215,"tags":[{"name":"sha256-88935f7cbad0f3dd32e7eec1fb72c2a4cd725b016265574fb579d8c3ae300608","digest":"sha256:9e19a2c01218a2e4de60ccaed14e9b02aaf459414d6d84f0ee1bb0151caef8aa","pushed":"2026-09-25T07:55:12.78141Z","size":7948,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"sha256-88935f7cbad0f3dd32e7eec1fb72c2a4cd725b016265574fb579d8c3ae300608.sig","digest":"sha256:23d73f6e267dd73b8764693f474c10ae6e6f7cf7ec1a619eb2b1f99c4ae62e0f","pushed":"2026-09-25T07:55:07.160562Z","size":249,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.config.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"sha256-1316462e269135135ae2aeea6d955b76aa7b76438b9bf54aab511a4176bcd6f7.metadata","digest":"sha256:88935f7cbad0f3dd32e7eec1fb72c2a4cd725b016265574fb579d8c3ae300608","pushed":"2026-09-25T07:54:57.121226Z","size":1924157,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.vmware.tac.metadata.config.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"latest-metadata","digest":"sha256:88935f7cbad0f3dd32e7eec1fb72c2a4cd725b016265574fb579d8c3ae300608","pushed":"2026-09-25T07:54:55.57888Z","size":1924157,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.vmware.tac.metadata.config.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"sha256-33b24031f6369ea2d1c906552d6f3edeb2c050a93caa3ff09b29cfc351501bbc","digest":"sha256:1d158690762a36ba1c62b400f3cce3d2001edee73b7088221eac6554313cae63","pushed":"2026-09-25T07:54:02.758309Z","size":7947,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"sha256-33b24031f6369ea2d1c906552d6f3edeb2c050a93caa3ff09b29cfc351501bbc.sig","digest":"sha256:2128fd9087c73d5f9de5c38e5db52435